# Local dev ports (Project F)

## Defaults

- **Vite (frontend):** `5173` — fixed in `vite.config.ts` with **`strictPort: true`** (no silent hop to 5174).
- **API (Hono):** `3001` — from **`PORT`** in `server` (default `3001`).

## What runs before `dev:app`

`scripts/run-dev.mjs` runs **`scripts/free-dev-ports.mjs`** after DB prep, unless **`SKIP_FREE_DEV_PORTS=1`**. The script can terminate listeners on those ports, then log what was stopped.

**Env:**

| Variable | Purpose |
|----------|---------|
| `SKIP_FREE_DEV_PORTS=1` | Do not kill anything; use when two stacks must share 3001/5173. |
| `DEV_FREE_PORTS` | Comma list, e.g. `3001,5173,5174` (default: `3001,5173`). |
| `DEV_FREE_PORTS_DRYRUN=1` | Only print what *would* be freed; no `taskkill`/`kill`. |

## npm scripts (repo root)

| Command | What it does |
|---------|----------------|
| `npm run dev` | Full bootstrap, then free ports (unless skipped), then Vite + API. |
| `npm run dev:free-ports` | Run `free-dev-ports.mjs` only (kill + log). |
| `npm run dev:ports-inspect` | `inspect-dev-ports.mjs` — list listeners, **no kill** (or “No listeners on ports…”). |

## Log lines the user cares about

Before killing, the script logs **port, pid,** and a best-effort line (Windows: CIM: **name, executable path, command line**). The **command line** usually shows the **project path** (e.g. `...Project F...`, `vite`, `tsx watch`) so the user can tell which of several local projects was holding the port.

## Manual checks (no Node)

- **Windows (PowerShell):** `Get-NetTCPConnection -LocalPort 3001,5173 -State Listen` and match **OwningProcess** to `Get-Process -Id <pid>`.
- **Any OS:** `netstat -ano` (Windows) / `lsof -iTCP:3001 -sTCP:LISTEN` (macOS/Linux) when `lsof` exists.

## Multi-project (3–4 repos)

Prefer **different default ports per repo** (set **`PORT`**, Vite `server.port`, `CORS_ORIGIN`, and Vite `proxy` targets consistently). For this app only, `SKIP_FREE_DEV_PORTS=1` when another process must own 3001/5173 on purpose.

